A||||3||Fret Naught||Tech. Q.||||1||
Z||000000||Fret Naught||05-31-2000||12:38 PM||||It rained last night, I get in my car to go to work this morning, push in the clutch at the stop sign and the engine dies? next stop sign it wanted to but I didn't give it a chance. Got to work and it Ideled fine. I am inclined to ignore it, but then I thought I should take a peak at the engine this weekend, just to see how things are going.<BR>Any thoughts on what I should check? It seems like I read in a thread somewhere that this was a common problem.||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||05-31-2000||12:58 PM||||Sounds like the classic "water in distributor cap" problem.<P>If there is water in the cap, it will be there until you remove the cap and dry it out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||05-31-2000||02:18 PM||||You could also have bad/worn spark plug wires. When I first bought my car it was raining. I opened the decklid to check oil level and such. As soon as the water ran down the decklid onto the wires the car died. I changed wires and no problems!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fret Naught||05-31-2000||02:54 PM||||I was thinking of wires, I don't much like it when you open the deck lid and all that water runs down onto the engine, are there any solutions for that? A after market gutter to install or something?||||reg||1
